   "unexplained_peak_ids": [],
   "reasoning_summary": "C9H8O3 has DoU 6: one phenyl, one C=C and one C=O. The 13C spectrum shows a monosubstituted phenyl: ipso 136.4 (7) and CH carbons 130.8, 129.3 and 128.4 (8-10). The 1H pattern 7.76/7.31/7.21 (1-3) fits the ortho/meta/para protons of that ring. The remaining three carbons are an acid C=O at 168.4 (5), an oxygenated sp2 carbon at 142.3 (6) and a strongly shielded sp2 CH at 111.6 (11). The vinyl singlet at 6.48 (4) belongs on that CH. Together these define PhCH=C(OH)COOH, the enol tautomer of phenylpyruvic acid. The absence of sp3 carbons excludes the keto form. The two OH protons are exchanged in CD3OD, so the visible H count is 6 of 8."
  },
